From: ahmedawachi <121810925+ahmedawachi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:07:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] cygwin: treat Windows drive paths as absolute in
 getAbsolutePath()

What: on Cygwin/MSYS2 builds, getAbsolutePath() returns a path that
starts with a drive letter and a separator (C:/..., C:\...) unchanged,
as it already does for a path that starts with '/'. Other platforms are
unchanged.

Why: redis-server stores its config file path through getAbsolutePath(),
which treats anything not starting with '/' as relative and prepends the
current directory. Started as "redis-server.exe C:/Redis/redis.conf",
Redis tried to open "/<cwd>/C:/Redis/redis.conf" and exited with "Fatal
error, can't open config file". The runtime itself opens Windows paths
as they are, so only this helper was wrong. The same helper resolves the
executable path and AOF directory paths.

A drive-relative path such as "C:redis.conf" is still treated as
relative.

Risk: very low; one early return on Cygwin/MSYS2 builds only.
---
 src/util.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/util.c b/src/util.c
index 3229b08..1950ddf 100644
--- a/src/util.c
+++ b/src/util.c
@@ -1042,6 +1042,11 @@ sds getAbsolutePath(char *filename) {
 
     relpath = sdstrim(relpath," \r\n\t");
     if (relpath[0] == '/') return relpath; /* Path is already absolute. */
+#ifdef __CYGWIN__
+    /* So is a Windows path with a drive letter (C:/ or C:\); the Cygwin/MSYS2 runtime opens it as it is. */
+    if (isalpha((unsigned char)relpath[0]) && relpath[1] == ':' && (relpath[2] == '/' || relpath[2] == '\\'))
+        return relpath;
+#endif
 
     /* If path is relative, join cwd and relative path. */
     if (getcwd(cwd,sizeof(cwd)) == NULL) {
